{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And they placed on it incense.</b> From their own. That is, 'and they offered before HaShem strange fire' — for it is impossible for incense without fire, and any incense that is not from the congregation's is called strange." "<b>Which He did not command them.</b> Meaning: which He did not command them to do, as it is written: 'and you shall not offer on it strange incense,' like the expression 'to burn their sons and their daughters, which I did not command them.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:01.386520351Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}